<section class="section" aria-labelledby="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="how">How I work</h2>
      <p>Four habits that show up in every project.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="principles">
      <li>
        <h3>Decide what better means first</h3>
        <p>What should change, in behavioral or business terms? That gets answered before design starts, so there is something real to measure after launch.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Smallest test that gives a real signal</h3>
        <p>Keep fidelity low until the direction holds. A wrong assumption found early is progress, not a setback.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Build systems, not one-offs</h3>
        <p>Design systems, content architecture and growth infrastructure should make the next decision cheaper, not need rebuilding next quarter.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Close the gaps between teams</h3>
        <p>Most product problems are coordination problems between product, design, marketing and sales. Having worked in each, I can see the gaps from both sides.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

